 comes  bursting out of the room rambling about  Bethany the flight attendant meanwhile  Mikayla on stakeout with her ex-fiance  Jared also experiences a hallucination  with the stone lady this time however  she isn't wet but has wings she speaks  to Mikayla saying save him which  Michaela confuses as meaning saved the  man on their stakeout this leads to a  bus gone wrong and a whole lot of  trouble for Michaela and Jared  as Salm V searches for answers about  Thomas she meets with Bethany the flight  attendant turns out Thomas's her cousins  lover who is doubling as a flight  attendant while trying to escape  persecution as a gay man in Jamaica when  they go to smuggle him out  Thomas escaped since on V and Bethany  rushed to find him before the government  does Sean V gets a clue from the water  footprints which leads her to Michaela  as they puzzle over where Thomas might  have gone Michaela and Sandra realized  they've been seeing the same  hallucination but with one difference  Sean V saw the stone lady with wet feet  and Michaela saw her with wings this  clicks and Bethany is the Angel of the  waters a statue of an angel on top of  the Bethesda Fountain in Central Park  this fountain is a big part of angels in  America appeal at surprise and Tony  award-winning play by Tony Kushner the  play also happened to be Thomas's  partner Leo's favorite play and where  they were gonna meet up after flight 8  to 8 was scheduled to land and lo and  behold there's Thomas at the fountain  scared and freaking out about missing  his partner Leo and five and a half  years of his life Sean V Michaela and  Bethany take Thomas to safety and  another calling is complete this time it  took both the callings of Sandy and  Michaela the different angels to work  together to solve it sound familiar all  things work together for good it's  becoming apparent that there's a  connection between these passengers and  that these callings are starting to pull  them all together likely for some  unknown ultimate goal where they will  have to unite for good just like they  all felt compelled to meet at the plane  and watch it explode and just like the  connection Michaela had with Shadow  victim Kelly Taylor and they are calling  on your truth but what's the  significance of the Angel of the waters  why this particular message and calling  I believe it was used for a very  specific reason the Bethesda Fountain in  New York takes inspiration from the Pool  of Bethesda and Jerusalem and more  specifically from an event called the  healing of a paralytic at Bethesda the  healing was an event that occurs  exclusively in the Gospel of John where  Jesus Christ miraculously heals a  paralyzed man at the pool along the  fountain in New York there are four  four-foot cherubs representing  temperance purity health and peace and  is referring to the Croton Aqueduct the  first dependable supply of clean water  for the city of New York it was and is a  symbol of Health and healing powers just  like the Pool of Bethesda was  to be blessed by God with healing waters  I touched on this a bit in episode 1 of  exploring manifests but could all these  passengers be in need of some sort of  healing or penance  could these callings be a way to become  cleansed whether it be a cleansing of a  physical ailment like cows cancer or  some sort of emotional burden  remember what Isaiah said to Michaela  last episode to unburden herself the  fountain itself also plays a large role  in angels of America a play which  examines aids and homosexuality in 1980s  America and is largely argued to be one  of the most important pieces of theatre  written in the 20th century many of the  characters in the play battle with AIDS  and begin to experience ghostly visions  and the appearance of angels the  character prior Walter is also described  by the angels as a prophet or carrying a  prophecy and that his mortal illness is  what has caused this prophecy in these  visions to manifest in him in Episode  two I touched on the idea that cow could  be some sort of Savior or perhaps now a  prophet at the end of the play the  characters gather at the Bethesda  Fountain and prior talks about the  healing of the paralytic at Bethesda  pool here the play discusses albeit  metaphorically the courage to face  changes despite not knowing the outcome  and the play ends on a note of hope not  unlike the characters are manifest who  are now experiencing great changes since  landing five years in the future and  certainly are leaping into the unknown  but more obvious is the fountain itself  a giant symbolic angel yet another nod  to religion in the connection between  these callings and a greater power  that's it for this week's episode of  exploring manifest I hope you enjoyed  the video and if you did make sure to  LIKE and subscribe I also have a Twitter  account where you can get updates on my  latest videos remember if you have any  new and exciting theories on the show  please feel free to comment below so I  can pull an olive and shove it in my  backpack to use for the next video

